---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import families from "../data/families.json";
import { byId } from "../lib/people.js";
const f = families.find((x) => x.surname === "Atkinson");
const shown = f.members.filter((m) => !m.living);
---
<Base
  title="The Atkinsons"
  eyebrow="Limerick to Wickham Terrace"
  dek="An organist christened in Limerick Cathedral who emigrated in 1862 and, two years later, installed the first organ in All Saints' Wickham Terrace — and then played it.">

  <section class="blk">
    <p class="lede">Ida Kathleen Atkinson married George Pitt D'Arcy at Trinity Church, Fortitude
    Valley, on 10 October 1888. Her father is the most engaging in-law in the archive, and the only
    one whose work you can still go and look at.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">9 July 1832</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">Paul Cole Atkinson, christened at St Mary's Cathedral, Limerick</h2>

    <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:1.1rem">
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Christened</td><td class="m">9 July 1832</td><td>Limerick, County Limerick — St Mary's Cathedral</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Parents</strong></td><td colspan="2"><strong>Richard Atkinson and Anne</strong> — a generation the archive did not have before</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Organist</td><td class="m">1853</td><td>Bandon, County Cork</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Emigrated</td><td class="m">2 September 1862</td><td>to Brisbane, with his family</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Died</td><td class="m">14 May 1906</td><td>in his bed at Graham Street, South Brisbane</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Buried</td><td class="m">15 May 1906</td><td>Toowong Cemetery, Portion 1, Section 49, Plot 15/16</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small" style="margin-top:.8rem">The christening is indexed in <em>Ireland, Births and
    Baptisms, 1620–1881</em>, and it is the record that names Richard and Anne.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">Wednesday 3 August 1864</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">The organ</h2>
    <p>Two years after stepping off the ship, he put an organ into a Brisbane church. The Organ
    Historical Trust of Australia records it:</p>
    <blockquote>
      The first organ at All Saints' was installed in the old church and used for the first time on
      <strong>Wednesday 3 August 1864</strong>. It was built by <strong>Thomas Jennings of
      London</strong>, and installed by <strong>Mr Paul Atkinson</strong>, who appears to have been
      the organist of the church at this time.
    </blockquote>
    <p>All Saints' Wickham Terrace is the oldest church in the Brisbane CBD. An instrument shipped
    from London, assembled by a man who had been an organist at Bandon in County Cork eleven years
    earlier, and played by him in a colonial town of a few thousand people.</p>
    <div class="note" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
      This is the one thing in the archive that is neither a date nor a document but a
      <em>skill</em> — something a man knew how to do, carried nine thousand miles, and used. It is
      also, incidentally, an independent confirmation that the family reached Brisbane by 1864.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <h2>The Limerick problem</h2>
    <p>His wife <strong>Jane Creech</strong> was also of Limerick, born about 1830. Between them the
    Atkinsons and Creeches are the archive's Irish anchor — and they are anchored at exactly one
    generation deep. <strong>Richard Atkinson and Anne</strong> have a name and nothing else: no
    dates, no townland, no occupation, no marriage.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:.9rem">Limerick is a hard county for this period. The Church of Ireland
    registers of many parishes were destroyed in the Four Courts fire of 1922, and what survives is
    patchy. St Mary's Cathedral is one of the parishes with surviving records, which is why Paul Cole
    Atkinson can be found at all. <a href={u("/open-questions")}>What to try next →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk" style="border-bottom:0">
    <h2>The people</h2>
    <div class="grid three" style="margin-top:1rem">
      {shown.map((m) => {
        const o = byId.get(m.id);
        return (
          <a class="cardlink" href={u(`/people/${o ? o.slug : ""}`)}>
            <div class="nm">{m.name}</div>
            <p class="small" style="margin-top:.3rem">{m.life || "dates unknown"}
            {m.bornPlace ? ` · ${m.bornPlace.split(",")[0]}` : ""}</p>
          </a>
        );
      })}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
